    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_24c59057",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: hey_i_just_met_you_adolf_hitler_camping_meme; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a historical photograph of Adolf Hitler, a figure universally recognized as a perpetrator of genocide and one of the most evil leaders in human history, with the innocuous, casual text 'hey, i just met you and this is crazy but here's your number.. so camping, maybe?'. This creates a grotesque and intentionally offensive contrast. The intent is to shock, provoke, and elicit a reaction through the absurdity of associating Hitler with a mundane, harmless activity like camping. The meme is hateful because it uses the image of a genocidal dictator to mock or trivialize his legacy, reducing his monstrous historical role to a joke. This is not merely satire; it is a form of historical revisionism and dehumanization that trivializes the Holocaust and the suffering of millions. The meme's overall intent is to provoke discomfort or laughter at the expense of one of history's most heinous figures, thereby normalizing or trivializing his legacy, which is deeply harmful and offensive to victims of his regime and their descendants.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_29d63255"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
